issue_context.body:
Tests marked with `.skip` and `.fixme` 
- both are skipped
- both are counted at the end as `skipped` 
- hides the number of tests to be fixed.

Having a big permutation of tests ( this mostly affects screenshot testing ) we skip a lot of them ( like some combinations don't make sense to test), but skipped tests are shown as `skipped`. 

Could be nice to not include the `.skip`-ed tests at the end, but only show tests with `.fixme` which are failing/flaky.
Showing both in separate lines also could be an option.

![Screenshot 2022-06-29 at 19 29 54](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7899764/176488690-9ec8364c-26f4-476f-b541-18a6f556b45e.png)

As a workaround we are doing this way, but meh
```js
    someStorybook.forEach((story) => {
        test(story.name, async ({}, testInfo) => {
            if (testInfo.project.name.startsWith("Desktop-") && story.name.endsWith("foobar Story")) {
                return
            }
            await page.goto(storybookLocalhost + story.url)
            await compareScreenshots(page, story.name)
        })
    })
```

